{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792758329,"nonce":"DM6zZLuH5+Jr5oAkBlKHLCiyXbE=","title":"Add extensible code-action providers and editor hints","message":"Build the shared provider architecture before attaching Run icons. Providers need language selectors, asynchronous request/response hooks, bounded data-only actions, version checks, cancellation, deadlines and ownership cleanup. RayScript extensions should register providers and answer codeActions.request hooks, with commands and atomic current-document edits handled through a central execution path. An editor chooser and gutter hints consume the same actions. Add a built-in Run provider as the first client; keep editor views and inactive documents out of provider caches. Exercise actual RayScript hooks, stale replies, capability revocation, lifecycle cleanup and UI execution.","files":null}]}